{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788362499,"nonce":"cE13HKEVK1DPBbCUy5GxH9qmf7U=","message":"This issue's own generalisation — *\"a floor satisfied only by pawns whose top\npriority lies elsewhere is a floor satisfied on paper\"* — has a sibling that is\ncheaper to hit and was live for the entire `m1-20260901` run.\n\n`WorkCoverage.cs:103`:\n\n```csharp\npublic int Have =\u003e FloorIsCapability ? Capable.Count : Available.Count;\n```\n\nEleven of the twelve essential rows floor on CAPABILITY (`40ed42f`: the game's\nown `requireCapableColonist` set — Mining among them). For those rows `have`\nnever consults `Enabled` at all. **A colony where every colonist is physically\ncapable of Mining and not one of them has Mining switched on reports\n`{\"work\":\"Mining\",\"floor\":1,\"have\":2}` and `ok`.** Doctor is the only row that\nfloors on availability, so Doctor is the only row where the enabled/available\ndistinction reaches the verdict.\n\nThe cap makes it unreadable rather than merely permissive. A FINE row is three\nfields by design, so `enabled` — the field that would have shown it — is\ndropped exactly on the rows that can hide it. Across `m1-20260901`:\n\n```\ndigest files with a Mining row : 55\nMining rows with NO enabled field : 55\nunion of Mining row keys seen : ['floor', 'have', 'work']\n```\n\n55 for 55, `ok` every day, while 128 `MineableSteel` cells sat designated and\nunmined and steel never moved off 33. The digest was not wrong — `have` is the\ncapability count and the capability count was 2 — and it was also never once\ncapable of showing the problem.\n\n\nSame read, same rows, same repair verb, same fix location. `outranked` (this\nissue) and *enabled-nowhere* differ only in which precedence step drops the\njob: one pawn ranked it below something else, or nobody turned it on. Splitting\nthem would ship two vocabularies for one idea — the mistake `927be4f` is\nalready open to undo.\n\n\n7. A capability-floored row whose `Enabled` count is 0 reports it — same\n   treatment as `outranked`, a named verdict beside `ok` rather than a silent\n   pass. `ok` keeps meaning the floor arithmetic, per item 2.\n8. The row cap must not drop the evidence: a row carrying either verdict is\n   never truncated to the three-field FINE shape. Prove it with a roster where\n   the flagged row would otherwise sort below the cap.\n9. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-work-rank.py` gains the case: a roster capable of Mining with\n   Mining disabled on every colonist, asserting `have \u003e= floor` AND the new\n   verdict AND that `enabled` survives into the emitted row.","files":null}]}